From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Johannes Stein <johannesstein@freeze-dev.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 10:38:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 094/115] Float invariants of a loop condition are computed
 once, under the same guard

"while (i < iter) and (tr + ti <= limit * limit)" multiplied limit by
itself for every test. optimize_loop_invariants now also hoists float +, -,
* and sqr of float constants and variables the loop does not write (unaliased
locals and by-value parameters, or main-program globals whose address is
never taken when every store in the loop goes directly to a variable) out of
the condition of a loop that tests first. A float operation can raise, so
only operands of short-circuit "and" are searched (never below "or" or
"not"), and the copy before the loop is guarded by the "and" operands that
precede it: it is evaluated exactly when the first test evaluates it.
tests/test/opt/tloopinv2.pp.
---
 compiler/optloop.pas        | 155 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 tests/test/opt/tloopinv2.pp | 100 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 254 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 tests/test/opt/tloopinv2.pp

